{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"submission\": \"submission.json\",\n  \"summary\": \"Submitted the corrected heartbeat-handler exploration after the first attempt failed to build.\\n\\nContext from the index: three findings are confirmed_in_scope, the restart check is accepted as a bounded negative, map v11 is the accepted basis, audit units are exhausted, and the previous exploration run ended in status error with exit 1. Its recorded failure was a build error, not a semantic result: the target RPC struct exposes its response channel as send-only, so the harness could not receive from rpc.RespChan.\\n\\nProduct contents (draft-relative submission.json with the corrected harness_heartbeat_shutdown.go, action=explore): the harness drives a single-voter in-memory node to the leader state and then calls the same handler the transport installs for heartbeats — Raft.processHeartbeat — with an identical AppendEntries request twice, once while running and once after a clean Raft.Shutdown. Each call now owns a bidirectional response channel, passes it as RespChan and receives from that channel, with a 500 ms observation window; the emitted heartbeat_handler_response events record responded, the response error, the elapsed time and the node state, so the running call (which reaches appendEntries and answers) can be compared directly with the shutdown call.\\n\\nThe question, the compared paths and the observation window are unchanged, and the failure mode of the earlier attempt is stated so the retry is not mistaken for a semantic repeat. This remains an exploration: unit admission is exhausted and exploration output guides construction without adding property Evidence.\\n\\nPreflight `validate` returned valid=true with no diagnostics. Acceptance and the clean-copy execution remain with the controller.\"\n}"}}
